# Security & Compliance
1. ZERO-TRUST: Assume all input is malicious. Use parameterized queries.
2. NO RAW PANs: Never store raw credit card numbers. Use network tokens.
3. AUDIT LOGGING: Any change to a budget, limit, or card status MUST be recorded in an immutable audit table.
4. DEPENDENCIES: Never add a new third-party package without explicitly asking the user first (due to supply chain risks).